Third-party Hatter algorithms
----------------------------

The hat geometry in crates/outfit-core/src/hat.rs is adapted from
Starbound Hatter by Silverfeelin:
https://github.com/Silverfeelin/Starbound-Hatter
Reference commit: 8a8d47314c639f84c50936bda61dfc198c39e49c

The upstream work is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 3.0
Unported License (CC BY 3.0):
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/
Legal code: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/legalcode

Changes include a Rust/WebAssembly port, direct PNG RGBA decoding, preservation
of alpha=1, shared lossless palette factoring and bounded compression
candidates, a dyadic coordinate canvas fixing bilinear boundary truncation,
and local UI/CLI integration. Only the stable, lossless hat pipeline is
retained; the upstream tiled compatibility mode is not included.

The MIT grant above does not replace the attribution and license notice for
these Hatter-derived algorithm portions. No upstream JavaScript dependencies
or example hat gallery images are included.

Third-party pixel display font
------------------------------

public/assets/fonts/Silkscreen-Regular.ttf is an unmodified copy of Silkscreen.
Copyright 2001 The Silkscreen Project Authors:
https://github.com/googlefonts/silkscreen
Source: https://github.com/google/fonts/tree/main/ofl/silkscreen

The font is licensed under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1, not MIT.
The full copyright and license are included in public/assets/fonts/OFL.txt
and distributed alongside the font in the static website.

The pixel interface frames, brand mark, equipment icons and action glyphs are
original to this project and covered by the MIT grant above. The artwork in
public/assets/icons and public/assets/favicon.svg uses original pixel grids;
no Starbound UI artwork or proprietary game fonts are bundled.

Third-party single-frame character preview
------------------------------------------

crates/outfit-web/assets/hatter-character.png and hatter-hair.png are
unmodified single-frame preview images from Silverfeelin/Starbound-Hatter:
https://github.com/Silverfeelin/Starbound-Hatter/tree/8a8d47314c639f84c50936bda61dfc198c39e49c/imgs
Original filenames: hatterCharacter.png and hatterHair.png.

These Starbound character images remain the property of their original
rights holders. They are used only as the fixed character/hair preview,
not as generated equipment assets. This project's MIT license and the
Hatter algorithm's CC BY 3.0 notice do not relicense the character artwork
or grant additional rights to it.

Character redraw implementation and generated layouts
-----------------------------------------------------

public/assets/character contains independently generated blank PNG sheets and
*-layout.svg label-only references. Separately, body-reference.svg,
front-arm-reference.svg, back-arm-reference.svg, head-reference.svg and
hair-reference.svg embed original Starbound pixel artwork with frame names
and aliases, derived from locally and legally supplied game assets with the
user's explicit permission to use those assets for these references.
The embedded game artwork remains the property of Chucklefish and/or its
original rights holders. Neither this project's MIT grant nor the Hatter
algorithm's CC BY 3.0 license applies to or relicenses that artwork, and no
additional rights to use or redistribute it are granted by this project.
These annotated SVGs are visual references, not directly uploadable editing
templates. Draw on the corresponding cells of the blank PNG sheets instead;
do not rasterize the entire reference SVG for upload or bake labels or grid
lines into encoded pixels. The separate two-image
Hatter single-frame preview notice above remains applicable and unchanged.
crates/outfit-core/data/character.json records independently derived frame
names, rectangles, sampled fingerprints and shared-frame constraints from
legally supplied game assets. These facts do not grant rights to the game's
artwork. The single-frame preview images remain subject to the separate
rights notice above.

The character encoder reuses the stable coordinate-canvas geometry described
in the Hatter notice; that attribution and CC BY 3.0 notice still apply to
those algorithm portions. Independently authored integration code and blank
layout artwork are covered by this project's MIT grant.

The community character-redraw technique was a reference:
https://github.com/FezzedOne/FezzedOne-Drawable-Generator/tree/fa9c0450b33b5634e53d133a25dc70dfb54e4a41
https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3071843411
No clear license was found for that repository. Its source code and character
templates were not copied or assumed to be MIT-licensed.
